.Dt LIBPOWERCMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm powercmp_client_open ,
.Nm powercmp_client_create ,
.Nm powercmp_client_close ,
.Nm powercmp_states ,
.Nm powercmp_suspend ,
.Nm powercmp_inhibit ,
.Nm powercmp_uninhibit ,
.Nm powercmp_inhibitors
.Nd client for the system.Power capability
.Sh LIBRARY
Power Capability Library (libpowercmp, -lpowercmp)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In powercmp.h
.Ft int
.Fn powercmp_client_open "struct powercmp_client **clientp"
.Ft int
.Fn powercmp_client_create "int fd" "struct powercmp_client **clientp"
.Ft void
.Fn powercmp_client_close "struct powercmp_client *client"
.Ft int
.Fn powercmp_states "struct powercmp_client *client" "uint32_t *supported"
.Ft int
.Fn powercmp_suspend "struct powercmp_client *client" "uint32_t state"
.Ft int
.Fn powercmp_inhibit "struct powercmp_client *client"
.Ft int
.Fn powercmp_uninhibit "struct powercmp_client *client"
.Ft int
.Fn powercmp_inhibitors "struct powercmp_client *client" "uint32_t *count"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm libpowercmp
 is the client to
.Xr BSDPower 8 ,
the
.Dq system.Power
capability provider.
.Fn powercmp_states
returns the supported ACPI sleep states as a bitmask (bit N set means SN);
reads are unprivileged.
.Fn powercmp_suspend
requests the machine enter sleep state
.Fa state
(1\(en5), which needs privilege the sandboxed caller lacks; the broker performs
it after a per-label policy check.
.Pp
.Fn powercmp_client_open
opens a session and returns 0, or -1 with
.Va errno
set.
.Fn powercmp_client_create
adopts an already held system.Power channel
.Fa fd ;
it consumes the descriptor only on success.
.Pp
The library speaks the FIDL protocol
.Sy bsd.power.v1
.Pq Pa /usr/share/fidl/powercmp.fidl ;
see
.Xr fidl 7 .
The first call on a session checks the provider's wire version and fails
with
.Er EPROTONOSUPPORT
for an incompatible provider before sending any operation.
Negotiation and the operation share one five-second monotonic deadline,
shortened by an active
.Fn service_budget_begin
budget
.Pq Xr service_runtime 3 ; on expiry the call fails with
.Er ETIMEDOUT .
Timeouts, transport failures and malformed replies
.Pq Er EPROTO
make the handle terminal; application errors such as
.Er EPERM
leave it usable.
Requests are never replayed.
.Pp
.In powercmp_protocol.h
and
.Fn powercmp_validate_message
describe the pre-FIDL wire records; they are kept only for compatibility and
are rejected by the current provider.
.Fn powercmp_suspend
fails with
.Er EPERM
when the caller's label is not granted suspend authority.
.Sh SUSPEND INHIBITORS
.Fn powercmp_inhibit client
acquires one session-owned suspend inhibitor, subject to the separate
.Va inhibit
policy.
It returns EALREADY if this session already holds one.
.Fn powercmp_uninhibit client
releases it, or returns ENOENT when absent.
.Fn powercmp_inhibitors client count
returns the global inhibitor count to any system.Power holder.
An acknowledged inhibitor makes suspend return EBUSY, including suspend
requests from its owner.
Release it before requesting suspend.
.Pp
Closing the client, client death, or provider restart revokes its inhibitor.
A transport or protocol failure closes the underlying session and leaves the
client handle unusable; free it with
.Fn powercmp_client_close .
The provider releases any lease when it observes the disconnect.
A failed call may already have reached the provider; disconnecting cannot undo
an operation already performed.
Policy errors leave the session usable.
There is no transparent reopen or reacquisition.
Check errors on subsequent calls and treat a lost session as a lost lease.
The lease does not prevent reboot, halt, panic, or suspend outside BSDPower.
Calls on a client require external serialization.
Clients inherited across
fork reject use with ECHILD; leases belong to the original process session.
.Pp
Typical use:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if (powercmp_client_open(&power) == -1)
        return (-1);
if (powercmp_inhibit(power) == -1) {
        powercmp_client_close(power);
        return (-1);
}
/* Perform bounded work; a lost service connection loses protection. */
error = powercmp_uninhibit(power);
powercmp_client_close(power);
.Ed
